  "prefLabel": "Asb 204.01 Declaratory ruling",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Asb 204.01 \"Declaratory ruling\" means a written statement issued by the board in response to a petition from a person to interpret and apply board laws, rules or both to the person's specific set of facts regarding a proposed action.\n\nSource. #7863-A, eff 3-31-03",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/asb100-300.html"
